# Native projects are generated by `expo prebuild` from app.json — they are
# build output, not source. android/ was previously committed by accident
# (there was no ignore rule, so a `git add .` swept in all 54 generated
# files), which made app.json silently non-authoritative for Android: EAS
# Build ignores orientation/icon/scheme/plugins/etc. whenever these folders
# exist. That drift was real, not theoretical — `expo-image-picker` adds
# RECORD_AUDIO through its config plugin, so editing app.json alone never
# removed it; only hand-editing the committed manifest appeared to work, and
# the next prebuild would have silently put it back.
# Regenerate with: npx expo prebuild --platform android
android/
ios/

